      "sc_TEI_bs:sc_PEI_bs",
      "sc_TEI_delta:sc_PEI_delta"
    ],
    "posterior_total_samples": 4000,
    "rng_seed": 42,
    "headline_metric": "post_mean_eta",
    "headline_metric_comment": "Per-species posterior-mean of (mean \u03b7 across cells), 95% HDI in log-odds units. We report \u03b7 \u2014 the GLMM linear predictor \u2014 rather than p = expit(\u03b7) because future TEI/PEI z-scores under SSP3-7.0 lie 5\u201310\u00d7 outside the Tier-1 training distribution (the future warming signal is ~2\u00d7 the 1901\u20132014 training delta), where expit() saturates near 1.0 uninformatively. Ranking by \u03b7 preserves the GLMM's authentic signal; relative-risk-style comparisons (e.g. n_cells_eta_gt_0) are more substrate-stable than absolute probabilities. See 05_outcome.md \u00a7 Limitations."
  },
